    "source": "HHS ACF OCS LIHEAP Information Memorandum IM2025-02 (March 3, 2025): FPG and SMI estimates, mandatory for FY2026 (Attachment 4, State Median Income by Household Size); FY2026 LIHEAP Detailed Model Plans for VA, CA, TX and MD",
    "source_url": "https://acf.gov/ocs/policy-guidance/liheap-im2025-02-federal-poverty-guidelines-and-state-median-income-estimates",
    "source_url_smi_table": "https://acf.gov/sites/default/files/documents/ocs/COMM_LIHEAP_IM2025-02_SMIStateTable_Att4.pdf",
    "statute": "42 U.S.C. 8624(b)(2)",
    "cfr_reference": "45 CFR 96.85 (SMI household-size adjustment)",
    "verification_status": "verified",
    "verification_note": "Retrieved 2026-11-17 by the documents pass on issue #18. Every one of the 612 60%-of-SMI cells (51 jurisdictions x household sizes 1-12) equals the table's 4-person value x the 45 CFR 96.85 size factor to within $1; a transcription error would show up as a deviation of hundreds of dollars. State choices are transcribed from each state's FY2026 Detailed Model Plan (heating/cooling/crisis/weatherization designations).",
    "assumptions": [
      "Poverty guidelines: the state plans' designation tables don't name a guideline year; the FY2026 federal tables in IM2025-02 are built on the 2025 HHS guidelines (us_fpl_2025.json), which this file uses.",
      "Income is annual gross household income. Virginia's plan states gross income (sec. 1.8); the CA, TX and MD plans' income definitions were not transcribed and are assumed to match.",
      "Income eligibility only. LIHEAP is not an entitlement: eligible households may still be denied for lack of funds, and benefit amounts vary by state, fuel, and household; neither is modeled.",
      "Maryland's percentages are applied to the state median income for that household size (the 60%-SMI table value / 0.6). Applied to the unadjusted 4-person SMI, Maryland's 1-person threshold would exceed the federal 60%-SMI ceiling, so that reading cannot be right."
    ]
  },
