    "min_pct_fpl": 110,
    "rule": "A state's income ceiling may not exceed the greater of 150% of the poverty guidelines or 60% of state median income, and may not be set below 110% of the poverty guidelines (42 U.S.C. 8624(b)(2)(B)).",
    "categorical_eligibility_option": "States may treat households receiving TANF, SSI, SNAP, or certain means-tested veterans' benefits as income-eligible (42 U.S.C. 8624(b)(2)(A)).",
